# The repo is authored on Windows but executed under bash (run_pipeline.sh,
# run_micom.sh) on WSL or the analysis server. CRLF in a shell script makes bash
# fail with an opaque "bad interpreter" error, so endings are normalised to LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
# Notebooks pass through v2/tools/nbstrip.py on staging: the committed form is source
# only (outputs, execution counts and volatile kernel metadata stripped), so running
# cells in the editor never pollutes a diff. Repo-local setup is in that file's header.
*.ipynb text eol=lf filter=nbstrip
*.tsv   text eol=lf
*.csv   text eol=lf
